  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The probability of a man hitting a target is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> The least number of shots required, so that the&nbsp;probability of his hitting the target at least once is greater than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> is....",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;(not hitting in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>&nbsp;trials)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;(at least one hit)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.9</mo></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>729</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math>&nbsp;which is true.</p>",
